============================================================================
SINGLE-SCALE DENSITY FLOOR for LRC(14) (13 speeds, threshold 1/14 = 0.07143)
============================================================================

(1) THE AP {1..13} (extremal single-scale family):
    M = 1/14 = 0.071429 (= 1/14, TIGHT); optimal witness t* = 1/14 = 0.071429
    good-density rho (>= 1/14) = 0.00000  (ISOLATED witness -> ~0; still LONELY)
    three-gap count g at t* = 1  (arithmetic orbit {k/14})

(2) NEAR-AP perturbations (bump one speed): rho stays ~0, g stays small, M jumps to a rung
    family (perturbed AP)      M          rho       g   
    [10, 11, 12, 14] (i=12 +1) 0.07692    0.02380   1   
    [10, 11, 12, 15] (i=12 +2) 0.07692    0.02920   1   
    [10, 11, 12, 24] (i=12 +11) 0.07692    0.03350   1   

(3) SPREAD single-scale families (bounded ratio <=13, random): rho > 0, g LARGE, M >> 1/14
    family (last 4 speeds)     M          rho       g   
    [19, 21, 23, 24]           0.20000    0.12740   1   
    [15, 16, 23, 25]           0.15789    0.10350   3   
    [21, 22, 23, 25]           0.12500    0.09970   1   
    [19, 22, 23, 26]           0.12121    0.09630   4   
    [14, 17, 22, 23]           0.11111    0.08040   2   
    [18, 19, 23, 24]           0.20000    0.13490   4   
    [17, 18, 19, 21]           0.12500    0.11060   3   
    [21, 22, 24, 26]           0.16129    0.11500   4   
    (spread families with rho > 0.02: 8/8 -- positive good-density, easily lonely)

============================================================================
READOUT for the Route-1 density node (single-scale residue):
  * NO uniform positive floor: rho -> 0 at the AP (still lonely, isolated witness).
  * The floor is a DICHOTOMY: near-AP (g<=3 arithmetic orbit, M a CF rung -- close by
    three-gap/rigidity, NOT measure) vs spread (g large, rho>0 -- close by decorrelation).
  * This is EXACTLY the domain my S52 coarse reduction leaves: multi-scale already
    grounded in LRC(<=13) (LRCCoarseReduction.lean); the analytic floor need only cover
    these single-scale families, split near-AP (arithmetic) vs spread (measure).
============================================================================
